            </returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection">
            <summary>
                Provides synchronous expert access to Linux hidraw input and output reports.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                Each instance owns a Linux FIDO native lifetime, but does not impose the typed connection's 64-byte
                packet contract. Construction blocks for worker-owned open, descriptor metadata and reactor activation;
                it neither initializes a CTAPHID channel nor changes process-wide settings. Reports are unnumbered
                payloads; the native seam supplies the synthetic zero report-ID byte for output only. The caller owns
                protocol framing, sequencing and recovery and must not interleave raw I/O with a session.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.#ctor(System.String)">
            <summary>Synchronously opens hidraw using the production report seam and shared readiness reactor.</summary>
            <param name="devNode">The hidraw device-node path.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.#ctor(System.String,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReportApi)">
            <summary>Synchronously opens hidraw using a supplied report seam and the shared readiness reactor.</summary>
            <param name="devNode">The hidraw device-node path.</param>
            <param name="api">The borrowed native report seam; this connection does not dispose it.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.#ctor(System.String,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReportApi,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReadReactor)">
            <summary>Synchronously waits for native open, report-size discovery and input activation.</summary>
            <remarks>Failure waits for cleanup of partially acquired native state; there is no constructor timeout.</remarks>
            <param name="devNode">The hidraw device-node path.</param>
            <param name="api">The borrowed native report seam; this connection does not dispose it.</param>
            <param name="reactor">The borrowed readiness reactor; disposal removes only this lifetime's registration.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.InputReportSize">
            <summary>Gets the descriptor-derived input payload capacity in bytes, excluding any synthetic report ID.</summary>
            <remarks>
                The native seam falls back to 64 when descriptor queries are unavailable. Supported capacities are
                1 through 4096 bytes; a successful <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.GetReport" /> returns the actual count, not padded capacity.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.OutputReportSize">
            <summary>Gets the descriptor-derived output payload size in bytes, excluding the native zero report ID.</summary>
            <remarks>
                The native seam falls back to 64 when descriptor queries are unavailable. This is metadata, not an
                exact-length requirement on <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.SetReport(System.Byte[])" />; direct output preserves supported caller lengths.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.GetReport">
            <summary>Synchronously receives the next actual-length unnumbered input payload.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Waits indefinitely for input, terminal failure or disposal; there is no read timeout. The owner
                transfers its exact-length array without another copy. This escaping array deliberately satisfies
                the unchanged <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.IHidConnection" /> contract: the caller owns it and must clear sensitive
                contents after use. Neither later reads nor connection disposal clear returned storage. EOF is a
                terminal failure, not an empty successful report. Only one ordinary send or receive is admitted.
            </remarks>
            <returns>A caller-owned array of the actual input bytes, without padding or a synthetic report-ID prefix.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.SetReport(System.Byte[])">
            <summary>Synchronously sends an unnumbered output payload, preserving its supplied length.</summary>
            <remarks>
                The array signature deliberately preserves <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.IHidConnection" /> compatibility. The owner
                copies the payload before publishing work to its worker, then clears its copy before completion.
                The native seam prefixes a zero report-ID byte and clears its own framing storage. This method
                blocks until native output returns; it never clears or takes ownership of the caller's array.
                The caller must keep the source stable during the call and clear sensitive contents afterward.
                Payload length need not equal <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.OutputReportSize" /> or 64; lengths up to 16383 bytes are
                forwarded, subject to native/device support. Overlapping ordinary raw operations are rejected.
            </remarks>
            <param name="report">The caller-owned payload, without the native zero report-ID prefix.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.Dispose">
            <summary>Stops admission and blocks for the shared native shutdown outcome.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Wakes pending input, drains held output and actual reactor quiescence, then checks close on the
                original worker. There is no drain timeout; an unproven release retains the native owner. Calling
                from the native worker or read callback is rejected. Prefer <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.DisposeAsync" />.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.DisposeAsync">
            <summary>Stops admission and asynchronously observes the same native shutdown as <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.Dispose" />.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Waits for held output, actual reactor quiescence and checked close. Close diagnostics can fault
                disposal after proven release; unproven release retains the native owner instead.
            </remarks>
            <returns>The shared shutdown outcome, potentially pending indefinitely while native drain is held.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.Type">
            <summary>Gets the generic HID type retained by this untyped report facade.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.ParseReportSizes(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Extracts input and output payload sizes from supported unnumbered YubiKey descriptors.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Uses the last nonzero input/output main-item size, with a default of 64 for each missing size;
                it is not a general collection-aggregating HID parser. Numbered reports are rejected.
            </remarks>
            <param name="descriptor">Borrowed descriptor bytes, used only during this call.</param>
            <returns>Input and output payload byte counts, excluding synthetic native report-ID framing.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidIOReportConnection.Finalize">
            <summary>Requests nonblocking, nonthrowing shutdown without waiting for or asserting native release.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReadinessNative">
            <summary>Synchronous poll/eventfd seam allowing readiness fault injection without replacing registration mechanics.</summary>
            <remarks>These are native calls, not async or hard wall-clock-bounded operations. Results capture errno immediately.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReadinessNative.CreateWake">
            <summary>Creates a private owned nonblocking, close-on-exec, non-semaphore eventfd or throws.</summary>
            <remarks>Never returns a borrowed device fd. Only this local notification resource may be retired on the poller after poll exits.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReadinessNative.Poll(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Native.Linux.Libc.NativeMethods.PollFd[])">
            <summary>Waits indefinitely for readiness and updates the borrowed descriptors' revents; returns ready count or native failure.</summary>
            <remarks>The reactor retains device references across the snapshot. No descriptor array is retained after return.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReadinessNative.WriteWake(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Native.Linux.Libc.LinuxFileSafeHandle)">
