        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidReportSizes">
            <summary>Extracts bounded unnumbered input/output payload-size metadata for the supported YubiKey descriptor shape.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxHidReportSizes.Parse(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Gets the last nonzero Input/Output main-item size in bytes, defaulting each direction to 64.</summary>
            <param name="descriptor">Borrowed report descriptor bytes, not report payload or native transfer-count evidence.</param>
            <returns>Input/output metadata with widened bit arithmetic and a 4096-byte bound per recognized main item.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Not a generic HID parser: no collection aggregation or global PUSH/POP support. Numbered
            reports fail explicitly. Retains the descriptor reader's truncation/default behavior rather
            than promising complete malformed-descriptor validation. Actual reads may be shorter, and
            raw output uses caller length instead of requiring a match to this metadata.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection">
            <summary>Provides the built-in typed Linux OTP connection over a hidraw feature-report native owner.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Selected by the Linux typed connection factory. Each connection owns a separate native lifetime with
                one dedicated worker and one ordinary operation slot; feature I/O does not use the read reactor.
                The synchronous expert facade uses the same owner type, not the same owner instance.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner)">
            <summary>Takes ownership of an already-open native lifetime.</summary>
            <param name="owner">The owner to shut down when this connection is disposed.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.FeatureReportSize">
            <summary>Gets the eight-byte OTP payload size, excluding the native zero report-ID prefix.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.Type">
            <summary>Gets the OTP HID transport type.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.OpenAsync(System.String,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReportApi,System.Threading.CancellationToken,System.IDisposable)">
            <summary>Opens a native feature-report lifetime on its dedicated worker.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Cancellation requests shutdown; failed or canceled opens await cleanup rather than detaching held
                native work. The native owner accepts the physical claim even on failure and retains it if native
                release cannot be proven.
            </remarks>
            <param name="path">The hidraw device-node path.</param>
            <param name="reportApi">The borrowed native report seam; this connection does not dispose it.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Requests cancellation of open and cleanup of acquired native state.</param>
            <param name="physicalClaim">An optional claim transferred to the native owner, not retained by the caller.</param>
            <returns>The caller-owned connection, which must be disposed, preferably asynchronously.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.SendAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <inheritdoc cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.IOtpHidConnection.SendAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />
            <remarks>
                The owner copies the eight payload bytes before publishing work to its worker and clears that copy
                before task completion. Native framing adds a zero report-ID byte. The caller retains its source
                memory and must clear sensitive input after the task is terminal; the SDK never clears that source.
                Cancellation before dispatch skips SET; after dispatch the task waits for native completion.
                The caller remains responsible for OTP sequencing and must not interleave session or raw I/O.
            </remarks>
            <param name="report">Exactly eight caller-owned payload bytes, without a native report-ID prefix.</param>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancels SET only before native dispatch.</param>
            <returns>A task terminal only after any dispatched SET returns and its staging copy is cleared.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.ReceiveAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <inheritdoc cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.IOtpHidConnection.ReceiveAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />
            <remarks>
                The worker allocates eight bytes for GET. Failed or partial output is cleared; successful output
                transfers to the caller through a read-only view and is not cleared by connection disposal. The view
                does not make its backing array immutable or automatically clear sensitive data: the caller owns
                that storage's lifetime and sensitive-data cleanup. Native framing uses nine bytes, including a zero
                report ID that is not returned. Cancellation after native dispatch cannot detach GET.
                For these built-in array-backed results, use <c>MemoryMarshal.TryGetArray</c> to obtain the owned
                segment, then <c>CryptographicOperations.ZeroMemory(segment.AsSpan())</c> after use. Clearing a
                separate copy does not clear the original. Do not apply this ownership assumption to arbitrary
                custom-provider results without that provider's contract.
            </remarks>
            <param name="cancellationToken">Cancels GET only before native dispatch.</param>
            <returns>A task yielding eight caller-owned payload bytes after native GET completes.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.Dispose">
            <summary>Stops admission and synchronously waits for the shared native shutdown outcome.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Blocks until an admitted feature call returns and checked close runs on the original worker.
                There is no drain timeout; unproven release retains the owner and any physical claim. Do not call
                from the native worker. Prefer <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.DisposeAsync" /> to avoid blocking the caller.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.DisposeAsync">
            <summary>Stops admission and asynchronously observes the same native shutdown as <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.Dispose" />.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Waits for any admitted feature call and checked close. Close diagnostics can fault disposal after
                proven release; unproven release instead retains the native owner and any physical claim.
            </remarks>
            <returns>The shared shutdown outcome; it can remain pending indefinitely while a native call is held.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidConnection.Finalize">
            <summary>Requests nonblocking, nonthrowing shutdown without asserting native release.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner">
            <summary>Owns the native lifetime shared by typed Linux OTP and direct synchronous feature-report access.</summary>
            <remarks>
            Roots itself before native acquisition and retains the original physical claim through checked
            release. One dedicated worker performs open, feature GET/SET and close; feature ioctls never run
            on the read reactor. Send and receive share one ordinary slot, with no backlog, replacement worker
            or replay. Operation task completion is not close proof. Unknown native/claim release retains and
            quarantines the rooted lifetime rather than allowing timeout-based release or a native-close retry.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.OpenAsync(System.String,Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.ILinuxHidReportApi,System.Threading.CancellationToken,System.IDisposable)">
            <summary>Creates a rooted owner and opens its descriptor on the original dedicated worker.</summary>
            <param name="path">hidraw path to open.</param>
            <param name="api">Borrowed synchronous report seam; not disposed by this owner.</param>
            <param name="token">Checked before/after native open; cancellation requests shutdown but cannot detach submitted open.</param>
            <param name="claim">Optional original physical/discovery claim transferred to this lifetime, including failed-open cleanup.</param>
            <returns>The opened owner; failed/canceled preparation awaits cleanup before propagating its error.</returns>
            <remarks>Preserves both open and cleanup failures. A held open/close can keep this task and the original claim pending indefinitely.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.SendAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Admits one feature SET and owns a payload copy before returning its actual operation task.</summary>
            <param name="report">Caller-owned payload (0..16382 bytes); typed callers separately enforce eight bytes.</param>
            <param name="token">Checked at entry and dispatch; cannot detach or abort a submitted ioctl.</param>
            <returns>A task terminal after owned-copy clearing and native return, or pre-dispatch cancellation/failure.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Admission takes the owner lock and rejects overlap. Caller source storage is never cleared by
            the owner. Native SET is attempted at most once, without replay or suffix retry; success may
            still succeed after token cancellation. The worker borrows only the owned copy.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.ReceiveAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Admits one feature GET into worker-allocated eight-byte storage and returns its actual completion task.</summary>
            <param name="token">Checked at entry and dispatch; cancellation cannot detach a submitted GET or free its operation slot.</param>
            <returns>Caller-owned exact eight-byte array storage exposed through a read-only view after a complete native GET.</returns>
            <remarks>
            Failed/partial staging is cleared before failure. Successfully returned storage is transferred
            to the caller and never cleared by this owner, including at shutdown. The view provides no
            disposal/zeroing API; sensitive output requires caller-managed backing-storage cleanup, and a
            copy alone does not erase the original. A successful GET can complete successfully despite
            cancellation after dispatch. Admission is locked, overlap is rejected, and continuations run asynchronously.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.Dispose">
            <summary>Synchronously drains the same checked shutdown outcome used by asynchronous disposal.</summary>
            <remarks>
            Retained for the synchronous expert facade and IDisposable compatibility. Prefer awaiting
            <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.ShutdownAsync"/>; submitted native work or close can block this indefinitely. Calls
            on the owner worker are rejected to prevent self-drain. Do not hold resources required by the
            operation being drained. Returning with an exception is not proof of descriptor/claim release.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.RequestShutdown">
            <summary>Requests shutdown for facade finalization without waiting for native work or propagating exceptions.</summary>
            <remarks>Takes the admission lock; does not promise lock-free invocation or acknowledge release.</remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.Linux.LinuxOtpHidNativeOwner.ShutdownAsync">
            <summary>Stops admission and returns the shared result of original-worker drain and checked release.</summary>
            <remarks>
            An admitted GET/SET reaches native return and public task terminality before checked close.
            Only proven native release permits original-claim disposal/root removal. Linux EINTR/EIO still
            report diagnostics after releasing the claim; unknown release or failed claim disposal retains
            and quarantines the lifetime. There is no timeout, native abort or close retry, and repeated
            calls share the same outcome. A hung native call may leave shutdown pending indefinitely.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime">
            <summary>
                The IOKit and CoreFoundation calls that govern the <em>lifetime</em> of a macOS HID connection:
                creating the device, opening and closing it, creating and releasing CoreFoundation objects, and
                registering or clearing the IOKit callbacks, and OTP feature-report I/O.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                <para>
                    This is a seam, not an abstraction layer. It exists so the constructor-failure and disposal
                    paths of <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.MacOSHidFeatureReportConnection" />,
                    <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.MacOSHidIOReportConnection" />, and <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.MacOSOtpHidConnection" />
                    can be tested without macOS hardware — the same
                    reason <c>IWindowsHidReportAccess</c> exists on the Windows side. It deliberately mirrors the native calls
                    one-for-one and adds no policy.
                </para>
                <para>
                    OTP feature-report I/O and checked close verify that accepted operations drain before the
                    physical claim is released. FIDO report I/O uses a separate bridge; this seam also exposes
                    the existing feature-report and callback calls used by the macOS HID connections.
                </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CreateDevice(System.Int64)">
            <summary>
                Resolves an IO registry entry ID to a retained <c>IOHIDDeviceRef</c>.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                The returned handle is a CoreFoundation object owned by the caller and must be passed to
                <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.ReleaseCFObject(System.IntPtr)" /> when it is no longer needed. Closing it with
                <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CloseDevice(System.IntPtr)" /> is not a substitute for releasing it.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Native.PlatformApiException">
                No registry entry matched, or the device handle could not be created.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.OpenDevice(System.IntPtr)">
            <summary>
                Opens the device non-seizing (<c>kIOHIDOptionsTypeNone</c>).
            </summary>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Native.PlatformApiException">The open failed.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CloseDevice(System.IntPtr)">
            <summary>
                Closes the device. Does not release it; see <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.ReleaseCFObject(System.IntPtr)" />.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.ReleaseCFObject(System.IntPtr)">
            <summary>
                Releases a CoreFoundation object previously created by <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CreateDevice(System.Int64)" /> or
                <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CreateRunLoopMode(System.String)" />.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.CreateRunLoopMode(System.String)">
            <summary>
                Creates a retained <c>CFStringRef</c> used as a run-loop mode name. The caller owns the result
                and must pass it to <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.ReleaseCFObject(System.IntPtr)" />.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.Hid.MacOS.IIOKitDeviceLifetime.GetIntProperty(System.IntPtr,System.String)">
            <summary>
                Reads an integer-typed IOKit property from the device.
