            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.IsExclusive">
            <summary>
                True when this connection holds the card exclusively; see <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing" /> for what a
                shared handle means. Custom implementations that do not model sharing report false.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.TransmitAndReceiveAsync(System.ReadOnlyMemory{System.Byte},System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Transmits caller-formatted SmartCard bytes and returns the raw response bytes.</summary>
            <remarks>
                This Tier 2 method bypasses <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Sessions.ApplicationSession" />, the connection session guard,
                and the logical exchange guard. The caller owns APDU formatting, chaining, response correlation,
                concurrency exclusion, cancellation recovery, and state integrity. Do not call it concurrently with
                a live session or another raw operation. Dispose and reopen the connection when state is uncertain.
                Keep borrowed <paramref name="command" /> memory valid until the returned task is terminal;
                only then zero sensitive caller-owned input. This applies to every implementation. Built-in PC/SC
                connections reject cancellation before native dispatch; after dispatch the call may succeed and the
                task waits for native completion and resource drain. Cancellation alone does not make a raw connection
                reusable; dispose and reopen if exchange state is uncertain.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.BeginTransaction(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
                Starts a PC/SC transaction. The transaction is ended when the returned scope is disposed.
                Uses LEAVE_CARD disposition when ending the transaction. Built-in synchronous begin and scope
                disposal can block without a bound on native acquisition/end; prefer async begin and, for built-in
                scopes, async disposal.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.BeginTransactionAsync(System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>
                Starts a PC/SC transaction. Built-in connections await native acquisition without blocking the caller.
                Their returned <see cref="T:System.IDisposable" /> scope also implements <see cref="T:System.IAsyncDisposable" />;
                use async disposal when available to await transaction end.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                The default for custom implementations calls <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.BeginTransaction(System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> synchronously and may
                block the caller; override it for nonblocking acquisition. Built-in connections reject cancellation
                before native dispatch; afterward the transaction may begin successfully, and completion waits for
                native work. Do not assume cancellation releases the connection or ends the transaction.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PcscConnectionNativeState.IsExclusive">
            <summary>True when the native handle was opened with SCARD_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PcscConnectionNativeState.DrainWorkerSteps">
            <summary>Runs queued steps until the worker is idle (returns false) or shutdown completes (returns true).</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice">
            <summary>
                Represents an ISO 7816 compliant smart card, visible either through CCID or NFC.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice.Atr">
            <summary>
                The "answer to reset" (ATR) for the smart card.
            </summary>
            <value>
                The ATR.
            </value>
            <remarks>
                The ATR for a smart card can act as an identifier for the type of card that is inserted.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice.Kind">
            <summary>
                Gets the smart card's connection type.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PcscNativeResources">
            <summary>Owns one connection's synchronous PC/SC resources and native calls.</summary>
            <remarks>
                This type provides no scheduling or synchronization. <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PcscConnectionNativeState" /> confines every
                call to its owned worker and does not publish completion until the native borrow has ended.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PcscNativeResources.IsExclusive">
            <summary>True when the handle was opened with SCARD_SHARE_EXCLUSIVE.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind">
            <summary>
                Represents the means in which the smart card is connected to the system or reader.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind.Any">
            <summary>
                Match any type of smart card during a query.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind.Unknown">
            <summary>
                The kind of connection used for this smart card could not be determined.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind.Usb">
            <summary>
                The smart card is connected through a USB smart card reader.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.PscsConnectionKind.Nfc">
            <summary>
                The smart card is connected through a Near-Field Communication (NFC) reader.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>Creates raw smart-card connections for an enumerated PC/SC device.</summary>
            <remarks>
                If <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> fails or is cancelled before returning a connection, the factory must clean up
                every partial native resource it acquired. If it cannot prove that cleanup completed, it must throw
                <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.UnrecoveredConnectionException" />; Core then retains the managed physical-device claim.
                Ordinary creation failures mean the factory proved its own partial resources released and permit retry.
                This creation-failure signal does not apply to disposal: any smart-card disposal failure remains unproven.
            </remarks>
            <remarks>
                A returned connection must not complete disposal until it has relinquished every native resource it owns.
                If disposal throws, Core cannot infer release from the exception type and retains any managed physical-device
                claim associated with that connection.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)">
            <summary>Creates and initializes a smart-card connection.</summary>
            <exception cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.UnrecoveredConnectionException">
                Creation failed after acquiring native resources whose release the factory could not prove.
            </exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IRegisteredSmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>Creates a smart-card connection while owning its physical registration.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Implementations accept ownership of the registration on every exit, including failure and cancellation:
                release it only after native release is proven; otherwise retain it and mark it unrecovered.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory">
            <summary>The built-in smart-card connection factory.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Custom factories implement <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnectionFactory" /> rather than deriving from this type.
                Configure connection logging through <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging" />.
                Without an explicit sharing policy, new factories snapshot <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />, initially
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive" />. Contention fails with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" />
                rather than retrying shared access. All built-in sharing modes request card power-off on release.
                Direct <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.CreateAsync(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.IPcscDevice,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" /> calls do not acquire the physical-device ownership guard used by
                <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Abstractions.IYubiKey.ConnectAsync``1(System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />. Coordinate discovery, including background
                monitoring, and other connections to the key for the full direct connection lifetime. With shared
                access, a discovery metadata read or another handle can select a different applet and disturb a session.
                Prefer <c>device.ConnectAsync&lt;ISmartCardConnection&gt;()</c> for SDK-managed ownership; the sharing policy
                still determines whether other processes can open the card.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing">
            <summary>
                The <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing" /> used by factories created without an explicit mode, including the
                one behind <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.YubiKeyManager" />. Defaults to <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive" />.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
                Set it once at start-up, before constructing factories or using <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.YubiKeyManager" />
                for discovery or monitoring. Existing factories and connections retain their selected policy.
                Migration: applications that require the former fallback behavior must explicitly select
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback" /> and accept shared card-wide security state.
                <see cref="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Shared" /> is also an explicit coexistence opt-in, not an isolation policy.
            </remarks>
            <example>
            <code>
            // Explicit compatibility opt-in, before any discovery or monitoring:
            SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing = SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback;
            var devices = await YubiKeyManager.FindAllAsync();
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor">
            <summary>
                Creates a factory that uses the configured <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.YubiKitLogging" /> logger factory and
                <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing)">
            <summary>Creates a factory that opens card handles with <paramref name="sharing"/>.</summary>
            <example>
            <code>
            // Explicitly accept shared access for this factory only:
            // Coordinate discovery/monitoring and all other connections to this key before opening directly.
            var factory = new SmartCardConnectionFactory(SmartCardSharing.Shared);
            await using var connection = await factory.CreateAsync(reader, cancellationToken);
            </code>
            </example>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing">
            <summary>
            How the SDK opens a PC/SC card handle (SCardConnect share mode).
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            Smart-card application state is card-wide, not per handle: NIST SP 800-73-5 Part 2 §2.4.2 lists the
            PIV PIN among the application security status indicators, so once a PIN is verified any handle on
            the card can use a PIN=ONCE key until the card is reset. By default the built-in SDK factory requires
            exclusive PC/SC access and fails with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" /> on contention,
            without a shared retry. PC/SC exclusivity excludes other PC/SC clients through the resource manager;
            it is not a guarantee about other transports or arbitrary custom connection implementations.
            All built-in modes request power-off on release (<c>SCARD_UNPOWER_CARD</c>) to clear card-wide state.
            Shared access permits other clients to use that state while the card remains powered;
            <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.ISmartCardConnection.IsExclusive" /> reports the acquired mode, and an explicitly selected
            fallback to shared access is logged as a warning.
            </para>
            <para>
            Set the process-wide mode through <see cref="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.DefaultSharing" />, or pass one
            to <see cref="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardConnectionFactory.#ctor(Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing)" />. Applications migrating from the former
            fallback default must opt in explicitly if they need coexistence with other smart-card clients.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.ExclusiveWithSharedFallback">
            <summary>Explicit opt-in: open exclusively; on a sharing violation, retry shared and accept shared card-wide state.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Exclusive">
            <summary>The factory default: open exclusively or fail with <see cref="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Devices.ConnectionInUseException" />; never retry shared.</summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.SmartCardSharing.Shared">
            <summary>
            Open shared, for applications that must coexist with other smart-card users (gpg-agent, browsers,
            the OS smart-card service) and accept that card-wide state is reachable from their handles.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Transports.SmartCard.UsbSmartCardConnection.IsExclusive">
            <inheritdoc />
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32">
            <summary>Decodes RFC 4648 Base32 text without creating transformed text copies.</summary>
            <remarks>
                Accepts ASCII upper/lower case, ignores literal ASCII spaces, and accepts either complete padding
                or no padding. Unused bits in the last symbol are ignored, not required to be zero. Empty text is valid.
                Other whitespace, impossible terminal symbol counts, and incomplete or embedded padding are rejected.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32.Decode(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Char})">
            <summary>Decodes Base32 text into independently owned storage.</summary>
            <param name="encoded">The borrowed encoded text.</param>
            <returns>The decoded bytes. The caller must clear them when they contain secret material.</returns>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The text has invalid characters, length, or padding.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.OverflowException">The encoded text's byte length exceeds <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Base32.Decode(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Char},System.Span{System.Byte})">
            <summary>Decodes Base32 text into caller-owned storage and returns the number of bytes written.</summary>
            <param name="encoded">The borrowed encoded text.</param>
            <param name="destination">The output buffer, which must not overlap the encoded text's bytes; unused bytes are unchanged on success.</param>
            <returns>The number of decoded bytes written.</returns>
            <remarks>
                Admission rejects overlapping storage or an encoded byte length exceeding <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />
                before decoding, leaving both spans unchanged. Once admitted, any decoding failure clears the entire
                destination, including any partially decoded prefix and unused tail. The borrowed text is never modified.
                On success, the caller owns the output and must clear secret material after use.
            </remarks>
            <exception cref="T:System.ArgumentException">The spans overlap, the text is malformed, or the destination is too small.</exception>
            <exception cref="T:System.OverflowException">The encoded text's byte length exceeds <see cref="F:System.Int32.MaxValue" />.</exception>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength">
            <summary>
            Utility for BER-TLV length encoding and decoding.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength.EncodingSize(System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Returns the number of bytes needed to encode the given length (1, 2, or 3).
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.BerLength.Write(System.Span{System.Byte},System.Int32)">
            <summary>
            Writes BER-TLV length into the destination span. Returns the number of bytes written.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Crc13239">
            <summary>
                Utility class for calculating and verifying the CRC13239 checksum used in YubiKey products.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:Yubico.YubiKit.Core.Utilities.Crc13239.Calculate(System.ReadOnlySpan{System.Byte})">
